---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'github', label: 'GitHub automation' },
  { id: 'gateway', label: 'LLM gateway' },
  { id: 'oauth', label: 'OAuth & native apps' },
  { id: 'dashboard', label: 'Dashboard' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Docs — MinhAgent" description="MinhAgent documentation: GitHub automation, the LLM gateway, OAuth, and the dashboard." fullWidth={true}>
  <div class="docs">
    <aside class="docs-nav">
      <p class="docs-nav-title">Documentation</p>
      <nav>
        {sections.map((s) => <a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.label}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <article class="docs-body">
      <header class="docs-header">
        <h1>Documentation</h1>
        <p>How MinhAgent's pieces fit together — and how to wire your own client to them.</p>
      </header>

      <section id="overview">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          MinhAgent runs as two Cloudflare Workers: a web app at <code>minhagent.dev</code> and a
          GitHub webhook receiver. Authentication is handled by Clerk; the web app also acts as an
          OAuth 2.0 provider so native clients can sign in and read your configuration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="github">
        <h2>GitHub automation</h2>
        <p>
          The webhook worker verifies each delivery's <code>HMAC-SHA256</code> signature against your
          <code>GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>, then routes the event into a Cloudflare Workflow. Point a
          repository or org webhook at the receiver and pick the events you care about.
        </p>
        <pre class="snippet"><code><span class="c-comment"># webhook endpoint</span>
https://minhagent-webhook.duyet.workers.dev</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="gateway">
        <h2>LLM gateway</h2>
        <p>
          Store one provider key (AnyRouter or OpenRouter) from the dashboard. Native clients fetch it
          over an authorized request and route model calls through it — the key stays in your account
          and never ships with the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="oauth">
        <h2>OAuth &amp; native apps</h2>
        <p>
          The native client (<code>minhagent-app</code>) uses OAuth 2.0 with PKCE, redirecting to
          <code>minhagent://oauth/callback</code>. After consent, exchange the code for tokens and call
          the API with a bearer token.
        </p>
        <pre class="snippet"><code><span class="c-cmd">curl</span> https://minhagent.dev/api/me/anyrouter \
  -H <span class="c-str">"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"</span></code></pre>
        <p class="note">Refresh tokens are single-use and rotate on every exchange. Revoking a grant from the dashboard invalidates its token pair immediately.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="dashboard">
        <h2>Dashboard</h2>
        <p>
          The <a href="/dashboard">dashboard</a> is where you save or remove your gateway key and review
          connected apps. Each connected app can be revoked individually.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .docs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 960px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .docs-nav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 4rem;
    align-self: start;
  }
  .docs-nav-title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .docs-nav nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
  }
  .docs-nav a {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .docs-nav a:hover { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; }

  .docs-header {
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .docs-header h1 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 680;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .docs-header p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .docs-body section { margin-bottom: 2rem; scroll-margin-top: 4rem; }
  .docs-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 640;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .docs-body p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 620px;
  }
  .docs-body code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.82em;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .note {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-border);
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem !important;
  }

  .snippet {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .snippet code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: inherit; }
  .c-comment { color: var(--muted); }
  .c-cmd { color: var(--accent); }
  .c-str { color: var(--success); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .docs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
    .docs-nav { position: static; }
    .docs-nav nav { flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
  }
</style>
